## Why This Is Asked
New angle: third-party feed integrity across regions; captures data lineage and external fault containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with lineage; - region-aware lifecycle; - logs/traces integration; - metrics for containment; - RCA and canary plan.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model outline
type CAPA = {
  id: string; region: string; feedId: string; version: string;
  evidenceUris: string[]; logTraceIds: string[]; t_incident: string; t_detected: string;
  containmentStatus: 'Identified'|'Contained'|'Investigated'|'Remediated'|'Verified'|'Closed';
  recurrenceRate?: number; mttr?: number;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate data-feed corruption to validate the canary rollout?
- What tamper-evident mechanisms would you add to the evidence store?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a secrets rotation bug with tenant isolation across regions, including data capture, lifecycle, APIs, metrics, and rollout controls.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing tenant context, vault/version, exposure window, evidence, remediation.
- Region-aware lifecycle with states: detected, contained, eradicated, verified, closed.
- Minimal REST API: create/update CAPA, link logs/traces, idempotent operations.
- Metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR per region, false-positive rate, time-to-containment.
- RCA template and canary rollout validation plan before global deployment.

## Code Example

```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  tenantId: string;
  vaultVersion: string;
  exposureWindowMs: number;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  remediation: string;
  state: "detected" | "contained" | "eradicated" | "verified" | "closed";
  region: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rotation gate cannot be bypassed in CI/CD pipelines?
- Which metrics best differentiate false positives from real exposures, and how would you alert on them?
- What logging/tracing strategy ties CAPAs to specific secrets and Vault rotations across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```
